  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating the way for an integrated approach to contribute to the SDGs and Green Recovery through Access and Benefit Sharing of Genetic Resources (ABS) - 2nd Tranche</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Engagement Facility aims to advance the sustainable use of genetic resources in support of the post-2020 Global Biodiversity Framework and the 2030 Sustainable Development Agenda in Asia and the Pacific. It will provide technical expertise and complementary funding to strengthen UNDP&#x2019;s existing ABS portfolio. In partnership with the National Institute of Biological Resources (NIBR) and other regional stakeholders, key outputs in the second year will include a feasibility study and resource mobilization for establishing a regional ABS Business Facility (TABF).</narrative>
  </description>
